# The directory tree now carries the distinction this file used to carry alone.
# data/source/ is irreplaceable and tracked; everything ignored below is
# regenerable, re-downloadable, or dev state. So these are whole directories
# rather than a list of filenames that had to be kept in step with the code.
#
# No trailing comments anywhere in here. `public/ # note` is a literal pattern
# and silently ignores nothing — see Gotchas in docs/build-and-deploy.md.

# ── Regenerable ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# buildings.geojson, stats.json, needs_data.csv, orphans.json and the tiles.
# Two minutes from data/ plus the cache; editor and public build share them.
build/
# Assembled by build_public.sh and deployed straight to the host.
public/

# ── Re-downloadable ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Geofabrik extract (53MB; GitHub warns past 50 and rejects past 100), its
# dated copies, and the cached Overpass response. All fetched again on demand.
data/cache/

# ── Dev state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# queue.json, the offline twin of the D1 submission queue, written by
# pipeline/server.py. Production submissions live in D1; this is never a record.
data/local/

# ── Local safety nets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# apply_queue.py copies data/source/*.json aside before writing. Git already
# holds every previous version, so these are belt-and-braces, not project files.
*.bak

# ── Working notes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A catch-up list of what is not finished yet, including which security headers
# are still missing. That is not something to publish.
CATCHUP.md

# ── Local experiments ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The era classifier and the one-off generators. They produce things the repo
# depends on — inferred_buildings.json, water.geojson, suggestions edits — but
# they run on a maintainer's machine, not in the build, and nobody needs them to
# rebuild the map. Local only, so this ignores the tree.
#
# NOTE: exp/research/ holds hand-labelled data (labels.json, the to_label_*.csv
# files, test_labels.json) that nothing can regenerate. Ignoring it means git no
# longer backs it up — keep a copy somewhere.
exp/

# ── Environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# wrangler's local cache — contains your Cloudflare account id.
.wrangler/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.idea/
.DS_Store


.claude